      "content": "The \"fiscal responsibility\" angle is okay, but the problem is the leaked memo specifically mentions he was told by the budget office that the funding was available and there was no deficit risk at the time. If a reporter brings up that specific detail from the memo—that he actually had the money but chose not to spend it—the \"budgetary constraints\" excuse is going to look like a total lie. How do we handle that specific piece of info from the leak?",
